from pathlib import Path
import json,re
R=Path(__file__).resolve().parents[2];p=R/'records/research/root_notes.json';ns=json.loads(p.read_text());D={n['id']:n for n in ns}
D['N23']['text']='The author explicitly leaves preservation of e) by F↦overline F open, while separately asserting idempotence of that operation. The local termination formulation on 023 and the stronger uniform e_n on 024 are later attempts to control this issue, not a proof that every original sheafification satisfies e). The further question about generation by closed members is recorded separately in N70.'
D['N44']['anchor']='une réunion finie de feuilles'
D['N44']['text']='The page invokes compactness and local connectedness of filtration levels for the finite-union assertion. The written hypotheses must be checked for control of the number of filtration levels and of the components meeting a closure. The context’s explicit local-finiteness axiom identifies relevant additional data but does not retroactively insert it into 031.'
D['N36']['text']=r'The definition exhibits the pair map \((U,Y\cap U)\simeq(N\times Y_U,\{a\}\times Y_U)\), and the NB asserts selection of an exactly ν-dimensional manifold direction. This is stated without a separate argument for restricting the manifold factor while preserving the required neighbourhood of the pair. The finite existence of a maximal order is a further assertion, recorded in N72.'
D['N39']['text']='Proposition B asks for a local pair decomposition with an immobile transverse point. The page gives no proof, and the literal a/N wording remains marked in the transcription. Constancy of the local normal type and dévissability of the factor are recorded separately in N73–N74.'
extra=[
('N70','020–021','self-flagged','ni que overline F est engendré par les fermés', 'MPL_147_138-190_transcription.tex, scans182–184','adds a second unresolved sheafification question','WG2 B15 (§1.2) [unchecked plan]; BISITE D.12 [Open, return claim]','The manuscript separately questions whether the sheafified family is generated by its closed members. This asks for a finite Boolean expression for every global section, an assertion beyond idempotence of sheafification. The locally finite and uniform-dimension replacements on 023–024 indicate the intended control, but the original question is not answered there in full generality.',['faisceau','local','fermé']),
('N71','031–032','unproved claim','corr. biunivoque par F↦overline F','MPL_147_138-190_transcription.tex, scans181,185–188','adds recovery of a leaf from its closure, used for incidence flags','INTAKE 20261114 §13.4 [intake lead]; STRATA C.5 [return claim]','The manuscript asserts injectivity of the closure operation on leaves and identifies the boundary with the union of strictly incident leaves. The proof obligation is to recover the actual locally closed leaf from its closure and the lower incident pieces, using the stated equisingularity data. On 011–014 the corresponding finite-partition statement was treated explicitly; the new version should be compared with that argument before its hypotheses are widened.',['adhérence','drapeau','strates']),
('N72','026–027','unproved claim','tt pt x de X a nécessairement un ordre de mobilité','MPL_147_138-190_transcription.tex, scans181–182','adds a finite-dimensional bound on local manifold directions','INTAKE 20261114 §13.4 [intake lead]','The finite-dimensional assumption is invoked to make the supremum of allowable manifold dimensions a finite attained integer. The chain-exhaustion statements on 027 use this existence of ν(x). The selected notion of topological dimension and its behaviour under the displayed local product are therefore required parts of a verification, rather than implicit consequences of the notation.',['dimension','produit','local']),
('N73','027, bracketed sentence after PropositionB','conjecture / unproved claim','ne dépend que de la composante connexe','MPL_147_138-190_transcription.tex, scans181–182,190','adds constancy of the transverse homeomorphism germ along a leaf','WG H4 [unchecked hunch]; INTAKE 20261114 §13.4 [intake lead]','The bracketed assertion identifies the local type of (N,a) along a connected component of Y_i. A proof must construct comparisons between the transverse germs of overlapping product charts and then propagate those comparisons along the component. The context supplies local-product/fibration goals, but no uniqueness argument for these transverse germs that settles this sentence.',['produit','connexe','germe']),
('N74','027 margin and028','self-flagged','N est dévissable?','MPL_147_138-190_transcription.tex, scans181–182,190','adds a transverse-factor inheritance question','WG H4 [unchecked hunch]; INTAKE 20261114 §13.4 [intake lead]','The margin asks whether the factor N inherits dévissability from X. The diagram on 028 proposes an equivalence for N and Y×N and points toward Proposition B, with the final sous/sans réserve qualification still uncertain. This records the author’s proposed route through the product assertion, without turning that assertion into a proof of its own needed factor property.',['produit','local','fibration']),
('N75','009, boundary NB','unproved claim (revisited proof)','dot A … est rare dans X','MPL_147_138-190_transcription.tex, scan181 (frontier condition)','adds a proof step needed for the boundary recursion','WG2 B15 (§1.2) [unchecked plan]','The author returns to rarity of the boundary after the earlier induction, restricts to its interior U, and reduces to a dense subset with empty interior. The cancellation and insertion history is significant because the density is relative to the closure, while the final claimed rarity is in X. This is the exact geometric step used again to make the recursive exceptional set on 015 rare.',['adhérence','fermé','local']),
('N76','033, admissibility itema)','reading question','la partition donnée de X_i est admissible','MPL_147_138-190_transcription.tex, scans153–155,181–182','adds a self-referential definition requiring a specified earlier notion','INTAKE 20261114 §13.4 [intake lead]','The live item a) repeats the word being defined, whereas b) specifies preservation of leaves under each arrow. The earlier F-admissibility on 014 and the cellular/equisingular definitions on 032 are possible comparison points, but the page does not explicitly choose one in a). The transcription therefore preserves the word admissible and the research formulation leaves that input unresolved.',['admissible','stratification','strates']),
('N77','036–037, source pointer','reading question / source lead','première lettre à A-Campo','MPL_147_138-190_transcription.tex, scans181–182; no A-Campo letter is supplied in the context ZIP','adds a manuscript attribution for the immobile-point construction','INTAKE 20261114 §13.4 [intake lead]','These pages attribute the intrinsic canonical partition to a first letter to A-Campo and propose paraphrasing it for marked closed subsets. The present package includes related immobile-point definitions on 026–028 but no letter heading or date proving that those sheets are that letter. The reference should remain a source-identification task, without assigning a date from the cote’s catalogue title to each internal section.',['immobile','A-Campo','A Campo'])]
for id,sc,kind,a,c,rel,reg,t,terms in extra:ns.append(dict(id=id,scans=sc,kind=kind,anchor=a,context=c,relation=rel,register=reg,text=t,search_terms=terms))
# Readable mathematical notation in the research prose only; frozen TeX is never touched.
for n in ns:
 n['text']=re.sub(r'\b(on|in|of|from|to|through|beside|into|with|at|before|after|for)(0\d\d)\b',r'\1 \2',n['text'])
 n['text']=n['text'].replace('type.','type.').replace('Q3','Q3')
 n['context']=re.sub(r'\bscans(?=\d)', 'scans ',n['context'])
 n['text']=n['text'].replace('V_i^circle',r'\(V_i^\circ\)').replace('V^circle',r'\(V^\circ\)').replace('W^circle',r'\(W^\circ\)')
 n['text']=n['text'].replace('the label PropositionA','the label Proposition A').replace('PropositionB','Proposition B').replace('PropA','Prop A')
D={n['id']:n for n in ns}
D['N59']['anchor']=r'\((\mathcal F,\mathcal G,\alpha)\)'
D['N59']['text']=r'The drawn datum \(\alpha:p^*\mathcal F\to i^*\mathcal G\) is sent by \(p^*\dashv p_*\) to \(\mathcal F\to p_*i^*\mathcal G\), by the unit followed by \(p_*\alpha\); the inverse sends \(\beta\) to the counit composed with \(p^*\beta\). These operations are inverse by the two adjunction identities and give the precise comparison with the triple-form gluing datum in STRATA C.6. The manuscript has not specified a higher coefficient enhancement here, so the comparison records this adjunction and does not silently change its coefficient category.'
D['N57']['anchor']=r'Il faut donc prouver que les \(\overline F_i\) … sont encore des “espaces”'
D['N41']['anchor']=r'\(Y_\nu(Y\times N)=Y\times Y_{\nu-i}(N)\)'
D['N62']['text']=D['N62']['text'].replace('∂_j'+r'\(V_i^\circ\)',r'\(\partial_jV_i^\circ\)').replace('V_j^circle',r'\(V_j^\circ\)')
D['N63']['anchor']=r'\(\partial(\partial_jV_i^\circ)\)'
D['N69']['anchor']=r'\(\partial_jV_i^\circ\to V_j^\circ\)'
D['N54']['text']=r'Bing’s nonmanifold \(B\) has a homeomorphism \(h:B\times\mathbb R\to\mathbb R^4\); the composite \(p=\operatorname{pr}_{\mathbb R}\circ h^{-1}:\mathbb R^4\to\mathbb R\) is a globally trivial bundle with fibre \(B\). This gives an explicit failure of the inference from manifold total and base spaces to a manifold fibre in unrestricted topology, through that actual projection map [Bing58,Bing59]. Our diagnostic has high confidence from the cited construction; membership of \(p\) in the selected piecewise category and the mobility values required to test 028 are separate tasks left unclaimed here.'
p.write_text(json.dumps(ns,ensure_ascii=False,indent=2)+'\n')
ctxparts=[]
for f in (R.parent/'context').glob('*transcription.tex'):
 parts=re.split(r'\\scanpage\{(\d+)\}',f.read_text())
 for i in range(1,len(parts),2):ctxparts.append((f.name,int(parts[i]),parts[i+1]))
audit=[]
for n in ns:
 hits=[]
 for fn,s,b in ctxparts:
  terms=[t for t in n['search_terms'] if re.search(re.escape(t),b,re.I)]
  if terms:hits.append({'file':fn,'scan':s,'terms':terms})
 audit.append({'note':n['id'],'terms':n['search_terms'],'hits':hits})
(R/'records/research/context_search_audit.json').write_text(json.dumps(audit,ensure_ascii=False,indent=2)+'\n')
out=['## Page-by-page research register\n\nEach item is separate from the frozen transcription. Context transcriptions are the supplied first-pass readings; their certainty has not been upgraded here.\n']
for n in ns:
 out.append(f"### {n['id']} — cote 121, scans {n['scans']}\n\n**Kind:** {n['kind']}. **Anchor:** “{n['anchor']}”.\n\n**Context:** {n['context']}. **Relationship:** {n['relation']}. **Register:** {n['register']}.\n\n{n['text']}\n")
(R/'records/research/root_notes.md').write_text('\n'.join(out))
print('Refined',len(ns),'research items')
